# Intra monorepo

Turborepo + pnpm workspaces. NestJS API, Next.js web, Prisma database package, pure-TS shared kernel.

```
apps/api        @intra/api            NestJS REST API (DDD bounded contexts)
apps/web        @intra/web            Next.js 16 frontend (Feature-Sliced Design)
apps/docs       —                     Static assets, generated openapi.json, diagrams, screenshots
packages/database        @intra/database       Prisma schema, migrations, seeders
packages/shared-kernel   @intra/shared-kernel  Framework-free DTOs, enums, constraints, rules
```

## Package manager

- **pnpm only** (`packageManager: pnpm@10.28.0`). Never suggest `npm` or `yarn` commands.
- Node.js >= 18.
- Add dependencies to the workspace that owns them, not to the root. The root `package.json` is a thin
  orchestrator: it holds pnpm/Turbo plumbing and shared dev tooling only.
- Cross-package imports use the workspace protocol (`"@intra/shared-kernel": "workspace:*"`).

## Running tasks

Prefer the root scripts — they delegate through Turbo with the right `--filter`:

```
pnpm dev:api / dev:web        start in watch mode
pnpm build:api / build:web    build one package
pnpm lint / pnpm format       across the workspace
```

Run a package script directly only when no root script exists: `pnpm --filter @intra/api <script>`.

## Destructive commands — always confirm first

`DATABASE_URL` in `.env.development.local` points at a **remote Render database**, not a local
container. The local Docker URL on the line above it is commented out. Treat the "development"
environment as shared and destructible.

Never run or propose these without explicit confirmation in the current conversation:

- `pnpm db:reset`, `pnpm db:refresh`, `pnpm db:seed`
- any `*:prod` database script (`db:reset:prod`, `db:refresh:prod`, `db:deploy:prod`)
- `pnpm docker:down` (carries `-v`, drops volumes)
- `pnpm clean` (removes every `node_modules` and `dist` in the tree)

The `:test` variants (`db:test:reset`, `db:test:refresh`) target `.env.test` and are safe.

## Environment files

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `.env.development.local` | local dev — **remote** Render DB |
| `.env.test` | integration/e2e test DB |
| `.env.production` | production (Render + Vercel) |
| `.env.ci` | CI pipeline |

All are gitignored except `*.example`. Never inline real credentials into code, docs, or commit
messages — read them through `dotenv -e <file>`, the way the package scripts do.
